# C8 TS with the COMPLETE ESTER BRIDGE in the QM region.
#
# The reactive ketone C128 sits in a dialkoxy ring:
#
#     O127=C55 - O61 - C124 - C128(=O129) - C120 - O64 - C58=O123
#
# The old 17-atom QM region held O61 and O64 but cut the ring at C55 and C58, so
# the ester arms -- which must respond when C128 goes sp2 -> sp3 on forming
# C128-O133 -- were held rigid in the MM region and severed by link atoms.
# This region adds the two ester carbonyl carbons and their C=O oxygens:
#
#     {55 58 123 127} added  ->  21-atom QM1
#
# Full system (no ActiveAtoms), TightOpt, OptTS + Freq in one job, seeded from
# the current full-system TS (../optts_full/job.xyz).
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS Freq TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  MaxIter 400
  Calc_Hess true
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
